WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.300
<i>A kingdom concealed in darkness, Deltora.</i>

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.650
<i>A royal heirloom, the Belt of Deltora.</i>

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.000
<i>Long ago, in this belt fashioned by the first king,</i>

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.750
<i>Seven gems were placed.</i>

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.600
<i>The gems possessed magical powers,</i>

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.350
<i>And were protected while the king's direct descendants wore the belt.</i>

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.150
<i>But, those gems were hidden in seven mystical lands.</i>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.100
<i>Since then, the kingdom of Deltora has been shrouded in darkness.</i>

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.700
<i>However,</i>

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.200
<i>The light of hope can be seen on the horizon.</i>

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:51.000
<i>Standing against the Shadow Lord, there is a boy who is on a quest to search for the seven gems.</i>

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.000
<i>With light and hope at their side,</i>

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.400
<i>They are off on their adventure.</i>

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:14.170
When I open this door
Kono doa akereba atarashii sekai ga

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.060
A brand new world is beginning
Ima hajimarunda

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.640
Even if there are painful things ahead
Tsurai koto ga aru toshitemo

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:31.040
I will show you that I can overcome them all
Kitto norikoetemiseru

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:38.800
I'm starting to walk in a brand new world now
Atarashii sekai ni ima arukidashita soko ha

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:45.030
And I'm sure there are [Dreams] and [Hope] there
[Yume] ya [Kibou] ga aru kara

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:48.250
This feeling is making my heart beat so fast
Dokidoki suru kono kimochi

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.380
And there's no one who can stop it
Darenimo tomerarenai

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:56.400
My heart is tightening and out of control
Kyun to hazumu kokoro

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.760
So start flapping your wings from here
Koko kara habataiteiku

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.810
And soar high up into the sky
Ano sora he to takaku

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:09.780
Aiming for [Tomorrow] and [The Future] beyond
[Ashita] [Mirai] mezashite

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.110
We will definitely grow bigger someday
Itsuka ookiku nareru to

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.380
That's what I believed
Sou shinjiteiru no

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:21.540
That's why, just spread your wings
Dakara tsubasa wo hiroge

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:44.800
The Japanese Deltora Quest is brought to you in English by ToranSubs

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.880
You're late! The arranged time has long since passed!

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.550
We're very sorry, but there's a complicated reason for this.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.990
Forget the excuses! You brought the food with you, right?

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.600
Yes, of course!

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.500
Just over there.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.450
The Ra-Kacharz are bringing the food to Grey Guards?

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.820
But why...?

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:19.600
My oh my, good morning Gentlemen.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.100
Isn't the weather pleasant?

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:22.830
It's Tom!

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.770
What do you mean 'good morning'? It's already this late!

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.290
Now, now, how about we have a drink inside for now?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:41.100
You're going to bring that food back to Del Palace after this as per usual, right?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.120
So how about a little rest?

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.090
Del Palace...!

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.870
So that's how it is.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:50.190
They weren't actually intending on throwing that food away, but instead sending it to Del...

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:53.680
...So that the Shadow Lord's
servants can greedily devour them.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.000
I give up.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.600
With something like that going on, I wonder what Tira and the rest would think if they found out.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.900
It's unforgivable!

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.850
The Shadow Lord, the Ra-Kacharz...

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:05.070
That's completely true!
The Shadow Lord, the Ra-Kacharz...

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.420
And even Tom!
That's completely true!

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:06.460
That's completely true!

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.400
That guy... He pretended to support the Resistance,

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.100
While in reality he was an ally of the Shadow Lord!

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.690
What was that sound?!

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:26.200
Come to think of it, that bird has been following us since we left Noradz.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.600
Oh?

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.440
This is bad. Tom knows about Kree.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.700
He might have worked out that we're hiding here!

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.100
Please do enjoy yourselves!

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:43.200
By the way, I'm very sorry to inform you of this,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.950
But you lot will have to return to Noradz on foot now.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.500
What do you mean by that?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.300
To tell you the truth,

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.830
The muddlets that I had prepared as your transportation back home were stolen...

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:58.470
...By three cunning travellers at that!

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.200
So it is true.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:05.480
Those three thieves came to the grasslands of Noradz too, pretending to be travellers.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.790
And, what happened to them?

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:13.400
We locked them up in our underground jail, for the crime of bringing an evil creature into Noradz.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.950
That's excellent news!

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:19.960
Well then everyone, feel free to rest in the room behind my store.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.200
I'll try to finish up my business in the meantime,

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.130
So that we can have a drink or two after the Grey Guards leave.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.840
We'll do that.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.500
What a guy!

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.440
Even though he acted all sympathetic with us before...!

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:42.810
Well then, if anyone wanted to get out of the cart in secret and move towards the bushes by my store,

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:45.000
Now would be the perfect chance.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.300
After all, Tom is the only one here right now.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.410
What does he mean?

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:53.100
He's telling us to move towards the bushes over there, right?

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.090
Can you really trust Tom's words that easily?!

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.390
But it's better to just do what he says for now.

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:00.200
Yeah.

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:10.850
Well then, I suppose Tom should do a little pruning for now.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.410
You... Just what are you up to?

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.190
Business, what else?

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.300
Business...?

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:21.250
I'm a merchant, aren't I?

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:24.690
Naturally I always have my customer's best interests in mind.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.700
You're just a liar!

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:32.000
You sold the Ra-Kacharz's muddlets to us as if they were yours,

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.900
But then said that we stole them!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:37.150
Lief. I know about how you feel, but try to hold it back for now.

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.850
Well, I am a merchant after all!

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:43.900
Of course I have to think in terms of my own profits.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:47.320
We had a real rough time in Noradz thanks to that, though!

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:48.530
But you see...

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:52.060
I told you to choose the left path, didn't I?

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.820
That way, the muddlets wouldn't recognise the scent of their home,

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:58.370
And would have no reason to go on a rampage.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.850
There's one other thing!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:03.080
Even though you act like you're an ally of the Resistance,

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:06.400
You're actually connected to the Shadow Lord, aren't you?!

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.790
It seems that you haven't realised it.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:16.290
My sign looks exactly the same no matter which side you're on, right?

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:21.300
Just like myself, whether you look at it from the east or the west, it will always appear the same...

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.450
No matter who it is I deal with.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:27.080
What's with this guy?!

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:30.420
I told you, didn't I? I'm a merchant.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.740
I'll welcome any customer,

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:35.070
And I will never pick any sides.

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:38.410
If it has nothing to do with me, then I don't care what it is.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.780
You traitor...!

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:45.900
But, it's all thanks to such a traitor that you guys can live on and continue your journey.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:48.370
In any case...

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:53.970
There's no one besides Tom who has noticed your
presence here, so now is your chance to leave this place.

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:58.050
And be sure to take all of your belongings as well as your garbage with you.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:02.970
After all, it's better for both of us if you disappear from here without a trace, don't you think?

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:17.100
Tom saved us, you know?

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.340
What else do you want from him?

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:23.040
There are plenty of animals in this world that care only for themselves.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.460
Tom is not an animal, he's a human being!

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.650
And a human should have justice in their heart!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.800
"A human should have justice in their heart", you say?

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.520
Really, your mouth is your only redeeming aspect.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.700
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.200
It's true, isn't it? Do you really understand it, Lief?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.200
What is truly just and what isn't?

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.800
That's enough, you two. This is no time to quarrel.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:49.780
We really should leave this place, as fast as possible.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.330
I'm...

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:55.260
I'm going back to Noradz to tell Tira and the others the truth.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.820
Are you serious?!

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:01.100
The Ra-Kacharz are deceiving Tira and the others even now!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.960
There's no way I can overlook it!

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.210
And what good will that do us?

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:06.440
Just think about it.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.800
Even if by chance the people of Noradz believed your words,

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.170
And they defied the Ra-Kacharz as a result,

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:18.000
The Shadow Lord would still attack them someday, meaning all you had done was increase the casualties.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:25.520
What you must do right now is reclaim the third gem by going to the City of the Rats.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:26.700
Am I wrong?

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.600
What's wrong, Kree?

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.610
Ah, you see a river, huh?

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.730
Is it close?

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.700
That's what he's telling me.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.940
Great. We'll reach the City of the Rats in no time after we cross the Broad River.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:20.400
It's the Broad River!

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:23.400
Amazing... it's almost like the sea.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:29.760
Is that the City of the Rats?

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:30.750
Most likely.

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:34.520
It's right in front of us. If only we can cross this river...

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:37.380
It doesn't look like we can swim across, though...

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.070
Having said that...

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:42.440
I don't see any trees that we can use to build a raft either...

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.420
What should we do, then?

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:47.420
I can't even walk anymore...

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.510
And I'm so hungry...

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:53.050
That's true. For the time being, let's have our meal here.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:01.000
Even after turning everything inside out, it's only this much, huh...

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:05.700
Lief, is there anything we can eat from
the things we bought from Tom's shop?

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:11.080
Don't expect too much, I doubt there's anything useful from that guy's shop anyway.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:14.250
Fire Beads, Light-Bubble Pipe...

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:17.400
Pure and Clear, and No Bakes...

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:19.970
No Bakes, huh...

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.820
Judging from its name, it should be food.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.330
I wonder about that.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.900
Oh right, I also have this thing that I got as a free item.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.150
Water Eaters...?

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.130
What in the world is this?

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:33.240
Is it a living thing?

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:34.280
Who knows?

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:39.800
"Scatter Water Eaters sparingly wherever land is required."

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:43.970
And? Are you telling me that it can even make that river dry up or something?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.100
I'm only reading the instructions!

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:50.710
But then again, I guess it won't hurt to try.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:51.970
Shall we?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:59.160
Water Eater, dry up this river and make land for us!

00:11:59.160 --> 00:11:59.940
There!

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:12.590
Nothing, huh...

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:13.860
What a letdown.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.100
Of course it is.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:18.500
There's no way that Tom would give us something useful for free.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:20.490
Wait, look at that!

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:34.400
It's a water pillar...!

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:37.510
Look, it's sucking the water from the river!

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.190
This is incredible!

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:06.520
It's a crystal! It's a crystal that can draw in water!

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:09.210
Amazing, it's keeping back the water around it!

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:11.130
We can cross the river now!

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:13.620
But, it's still one of Tom's products...

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.700
Can we really trust it...?

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:19.000
What, are you scared to cross now?

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.690
That's obviously not true!

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.000
Are you alright, Lief?

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:27.950
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:33.370
It's a little bit muddy, but it's not too slippery to walk.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.090
Lief, throw some more.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.020
Yeah.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.190
It's just like magic...

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.490
I didn't know such a convenient thing existed.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.810
Good, let's pick up the pace.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.440
But, I don't think there's much left.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:18.610
I wonder if it's enough to get us to the shore...

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:19.900
Huh?
Eh?

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:23.700
Listen here, say something that important earlier, would you?!

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:27.700
Now what?

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.080
The pillars are crumbling!

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:37.970
It's coming this way!

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:38.800
Run!

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:43.660
Just what is happening here?!

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:47.560
It's written here that the effect will not last very long... Huh?!

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:50.970
Geez, this is why you have to say this stuff sooner!

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:52.290
Anyway, get moving!

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:55.570
Don't look back!

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:20.770
We're really lucky, aren't we...

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:21.910
Yeah.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:23.370
Thanks to the belt, probably...

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:26.640
Really now?

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:29.720
It was also because of that belt that we went through that, though.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.650
But we did arrive here, didn't we?

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.400
That really was tiring.

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:41.710
Moreover, we didn't even get a chance to eat earlier.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.860
I just want to sleep for now...

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:47.050
But the City of the Rats is right in front of us!

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.810
Wait, you're telling us to go right away?!

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:51.990
Yeah, let's go.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.900
Hold on, why are you in such a rush?

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:57.610
The third gem is right before our eyes, you know!

00:15:57.610 --> 00:15:59.360
Of course I will be in a rush!

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:04.000
Will things really change once you get your hands on the gem, I wonder?

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.440
What do you mean by that?

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:09.720
Then tell me, Lief, how exactly will our lives change after we've gathered the gems?

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:10.930
That's...

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:13.280
Come, let's just eat for now.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.670
I'm so hungry that I can't take another step.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.180
I want to dry my clothes too.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:21.500
Oh right, Lief, among the things we bought from Tom,

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.800
There's something called 'Fire Beads' too, right?

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:25.730
I think we could use those now.

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:27.600
You're going to rely on Tom again?

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.860
We have no other choice here.

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.440
Besides, the Water Eaters were pretty useful.

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:37.430
We only went through all of that because a certain someone didn't read the instructions properly!

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:40.800
Fine...

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:46.700
Let's see here... "Hit with hard object to ignite", huh...

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:50.640
Ouch, ouch!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.480
Wow, it really makes a fire!

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:59.210
This is great! Now I just need to throw one more and...

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:04.120
I'm sure my clothes will dry up in no time now!

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.890
Lief, hand over the No Bakes too!

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:08.290
I'm certain we can eat it!

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:11.200
Here.

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:16.570
It doesn't really look edible as it is though...

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:19.450
It seems like it will turn into bread with some water.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:20.380
Water...?

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:25.500
Is this enough?

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:26.300
Yeah.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:30.980
Pure and Clear... If it truly lives up to its name,

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.300
Then it should be able to make this water drinkable.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:41.590
It's really clearing up!

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.300
I'll pour it over them now!

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:48.090
They're swelling up!

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:51.160
This is incredible! They really became loaves of bread!

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:54.570
Delicious!

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.560
Yeah, not bad at all.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.550
What's wrong, Lief? You're not hungry?

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.830
Nope, not at all!

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:03.080
How stubborn.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.990
I'm really not hungry!

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:09.300
At least your stomach is being honest.

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:11.150
Oh, shut up!

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:11.800
Here.

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:14.400
Eat up, it's really good.

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:22.660
You can hate Tom, but his products have done nothing wrong.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:26.610
That's right. You won't live a long life if you're too stubborn, you know?

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.340
What's that?

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.260
They're rats!

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.170
Rats?!

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:47.420
The whole lot of them?!

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:48.850
Let's run!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:49.630
Where?!

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:52.400
The river! There's no other choice!

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:55.710
Oh right! Don't forget to wear the Ra-Kacharz clothes too!

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:10.610
What's with this huge group of rats?

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:13.810
They're coming this way!

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:16.090
Be careful, these things will bite!

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:22.290
Stay away!

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:23.400
Jasmine!

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.360
Shit...!

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:32.210
A new wave is coming! It won't end well at this rate!

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.400
Oh yeah, let's use that!

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:45.810
Alright!

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.200
They're still coming?

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:52.210
Take this!

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:57.700
Let's move upstream while the wall of fire slows them down!

00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:58.200
Right.

00:19:58.200 --> 00:19:59.180
Okay!

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:07.000
Damn it! This is all that's left?

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.700
I can't move anymore...

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:27.250
To think that we'd owe our lives to these Ra-Kacharz clothes...

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:30.800
The rats were probably repelled by the mushrooms too.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:33.880
Clean Noradzeer...

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:34.580
Hmm?

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:36.900
What's gotten into you?

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:38.990
Clean Noradzeer...

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.600
Could it be that this gesture...

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.730
Actually originated from a gesture to drive away rats?

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:46.060
What do you mean?

00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:49.580
I think Noradz was originally the City of the Rats,

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:53.300
But, they were attacked by the rats and were forced to flee from their own city...

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.660
What makes you say that?

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:56.860
That symbol.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:57.640
Hmm?

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:03.380
It's really similar to what I've seen several times in Noradz.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:10.970
Now that you mention it, you're right...

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:14.380
And they were probably scared of Filli because he's similar to a rat.

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:21.800
I see. They're so obsessed with cleanliness because they don't want any rats near them...

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:28.990
Yeah. And it's also possible that the Ra-Kacharz were wearing those red clothes to protect the people from the rats.

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:32.090
That's why they were so worshipped by the citizens.

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:35.700
It seems like your reasoning might be right on the mark.

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:39.340
And the Ra-Kacharz are actually the Shadow Lord's followers.

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:43.460
In other words, Noradz is actually a city that the Shadow Lord saved!

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:44.300
I see...

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:51.600
The reason why they don't revolt is because they owe their lives to the Shadow Lord.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:59.870
We should wear these when we enter the City of the Rats.

00:21:59.870 --> 00:22:01.140
You're right.

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:04.160
I bet there are still tonnes of rats hiding inside that city.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:09.850
Even after you went through all that, you're still going to the City of the Rats?

00:22:09.850 --> 00:22:12.770
The third gem is hidden there after all!

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:18.770
Sorry, but I can't go any further.

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.050
I'm thinking...

00:22:23.050 --> 00:22:25.800
To end my journey in this place.

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:27.600
Jasmine...

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:41.250
Cherry blossom flowers are fluttering down
Sakura maiochite yuku

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:46.920
As if they were peeled from the sky
Sora kara hagareru you ni

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:52.880
I'm gripping and holding hard
Anata to ita omoide ha

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:58.650
The memories I have with you
Zutto gyutto dakishimeteru kara

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:05.950
All of a sudden, flower petals are in full bloom
Futto maue ni ukabu no ha

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:09.550
They're floating right above me
Mankai no hanabira

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:17.330
No matter how long I wait, no one is coming
Mattetatte mou daremo konai

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:24.300
Have I really left my wavering feelings behind?
Yureru omoi ha oitekitandeshou

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:32.540
I'm all alone right here, singing a song about cherry blossoms
Sakura uta utai nagara

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:38.480
Just waiting for no one else but you
Anata wo matsu watashi ha hitori

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:44.490
This love has taught something to me:
Kono koi ga oshiete kureta

00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:50.800
That true love is hidden on ordinary days
Heibon na hibi koso ai to

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:59.010
I present my last song to the spring breeze
Harukaze ni saigo no uta wo

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:07.930
Tom's Shop.

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:14.610
It's a shop that has a lot of useful things for travelling, like Water Eaters and Fire Beads.

00:24:14.920 --> 00:24:19.000
You can get free items, but no merchandise can be returned.

00:24:20.220 --> 00:24:26.760
Not long after we survived an attack from a huge group of rats, we parted ways with Jasmine who wanted to end her journey.

00:24:26.760 --> 00:24:30.490
And then I followed a mysterious voice which turned out to be the gem's guardian, Reeah!

00:24:30.490 --> 00:24:31.800
The King of the City of the Rats

00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:34.450
Next time, 'The King of the City of the Rats!'.
